<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 10_flexbox/17: Equal-height cards -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Equal-height cards</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .cards { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .card { flex: 1 1 14rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.25rem; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08); }
    .card p { flex: 1; }
    .card a { align-self: flex-start; background: #0f172a; color: #fff; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Equal-height cards</h1>
    <p class="lead">Cards in a row stretch to the tallest, buttons pinned to the bottom.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card"><h2>Starter</h2><p>Short text.</p><a href="#s">Choose</a></article>
      <article class="card"><h2>Growth</h2><p>A much longer description that wraps onto several lines and makes this card taller than the others in the row.</p><a href="#g">Choose</a></article>
      <article class="card"><h2>Scale</h2><p>Medium length text here.</p><a href="#c">Choose</a></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
